FreeBSD notes for misc/deepseek-harness 0.2.2-rc.2
==================================================

The port starts from the upstream source archive, fetched with USE_GITHUB:

  https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/archive/refs/tags/dsh-v0.2.2-rc.2.tar.gz

All FreeBSD changes are confined to files/:

  patch-native_system_packages_entry_src_flock.ts
      Teach the lazy flock entry that FreeBSD is a supported host.

  patch-native_system_scripts_build.ts
      Build the Node-API flock addon with the system C compiler. The
      Landlock launcher is Linux-only and is not part of this port.

  patch-packages_subprocess_subprocess-local_src_process-inspector.ts
      Provide a ps(1) based inspector. FreeBSD calls the session keyword
      "sid" and needs each -o keyword passed separately; its state field
      can carry trailing flag letters.

  patch-packages_terminal_terminal-bash_src_config.ts
      Use /usr/local/bin/bash, the location installed by shells/bash.

  patch-packages_util_ripgrep_src_index.ts
      Resolve the system ripgrep when no @vscode/ripgrep binary exists.
      No FreeBSD binary is shipped by that package.

  patch-packages_boot_app-boot_src_profile-resolution_resolver.ts
      When --expose-internals is active, load Node's internal ESM/CJS
      loader modules through require(). This avoids the unavailable
      node-addon-require-builtin binding on FreeBSD.

  freebsd-x64/
      The @deepseek-ai/node-addon-system-freebsd-x64 workspace package:
      package.json, prebuilds.json and a short README. post-extract copies
      it into native/system/packages/freebsd-x64.

  packagejsons/
      The root package.json, pnpm-workspace.yaml, pnpm-lock.yaml and the
      pnpm patches/ directory needed by USES=npm:pnpm,fetch, plus the two
      manifests changed for FreeBSD: the optional freebsd-x64 dependency
      of the native entry and the freebsd-x64 workspace package. All other
      workspace manifests come directly from the upstream archive.

  fix-deploy-links.py
      Copy the two link: vendor packages into the deploy tree, remove links
      that escape it, and rename workspace virtual-store directories from
      pkg@file++++<absolute build path> to pkg@file+workspace. Rewriting
      those names is what keeps pkg-plist independent of WRKSRC.

Dependency handling
-------------------

The workspace contains roughly 1,700 package entries. Fetching them during
build would require network access and would run install scripts before the
FreeBSD patches are applied. The port therefore uses:

  USES=npm:pnpm,fetch
  NPM_PREFETCH=yes
  NPM_EXTRACT=no

make fetch runs pnpm fetch against the manifests in files/packagejsons and
archives the result as deepseek-harness-0.2.2-rc.2-node-modules-x64.tar.gz.
make build restores the normalized store index with sqlite3, then runs
pnpm install --offline --frozen-lockfile --trust-lockfile. No registry
request is made during the build.

do-build then emits the host libraries, client bundles and Web assets, and
creates a production deploy from python/sdk-runtime. The deploy root is the
upstream maintained "all host packages" closure. The Electron desktop bundle
is intentionally skipped.

The deploy keeps relative symlinks, so do-install copies node_modules with
cp -R rather than dereferencing it. A minimal package.json is written at
${PREFIX}/lib/node_modules/deepseek-harness, and ${PREFIX}/bin/dsh launches
node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/lib/bin.js.

Native code
-----------

  node-pty        built by node-gyp with the system compiler and
                  /usr/local/include/node; the patch adds closefrom(3).
  flock addon     compiled from native/system/packages/entry/src/flock.c
                  by native/system/scripts/build.ts.
  koffi           uses the upstream @koromix/koffi-freebsd-x64 prebuilt
                  binary; no other platform binary is installed.
  ripgrep         @vscode/ripgrep has no FreeBSD binary. The patched
                  resolver falls back to the ripgrep installed by
                  textproc/ripgrep.
  esbuild         build-only. devel/esbuild exists, but the workspace locks
                  0.21.5, 0.25.12, 0.28.1 and 0.28.2; one system binary cannot
                  serve every locked JavaScript API, so the platform packages
                  stay confined to the build tree.

The non-FreeBSD node-pty prebuilds are deleted from the deploy tree before
installation. The only loadable native objects in the package are built on
FreeBSD or are the FreeBSD koffi binary.

Service and sandbox
-------------------

files/dsh_web.in is a conventional rc.subr script. It runs as www, keeps
DSH_HOME in /var/db/dsh, writes the pidfile there, waits for the token line
in the log, and uses the installed path for stop/status matching.
dsh_web_env and dsh_web_env_file are handled by rc.subr itself.

The port does not ship a sandbox backend. The launcher defaults
DSH_PERMISSION_MODE to danger-full-access so the CLI and Web UI are usable;
workspace-write remains available only when a compatible backend exists.

Account sign-in
---------------

The DeepSeek account provider accepts only a loopback HTTP origin for the
OAuth callback (RFC 8252 style). If the browser opens the UI at
http://10.0.0.3:3080, startSignIn rejects that origin before opening the
authorization page and the UI reports a failed login. The /api trust fence
and --trusted-host do not change this account-specific rule.

Use an SSH local forward and open the loopback URL:

  ssh -N -L 3080:10.0.0.3:3080 <user>@<host>
  # browser: http://127.0.0.1:3080/?token=<token>

The Platform redirect then goes to 127.0.0.1:3080/oauth/callback on the
client, through the tunnel to the waiting listener. An API key configured
in Settings or supplied through DEEPSEEK_API_KEY avoids the loopback
constraint and is sufficient for model use; account sign-in is needed only
for profile, balance and bonus features.

Verification
------------

Completed on FreeBSD 15.1 amd64 with Node 24:

  dsh --version                0.2.2-rc.2
  dsh --help                   identical to the source launcher
  dsh web --help               installed wrapper matches the source entry;
                               the source launcher needs the same
                               --expose-internals flag to boot the host
  dsh web                      token URL, HTTP 200 from the Web UI
  dsh headless                 mock LLM turn completed; bash tool output
                               and session files written under DSH_HOME
  native flock                 second lock rejected with EAGAIN
  process inspector            snapshot/tree/isAlive/session against ps(1)
  package install              wrapper and native addons load from the
                               installed lib/node_modules tree
